# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the EggSaminer Next.js project following the official Vercel documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Package**: `@vercel/speed-insights` v2.0.0
- **Package Manager**: npm
- **Command**: `npm install @vercel/speed-insights`

### 2. Files Modified

#### `app/layout.tsx`
- Added import for `SpeedInsights` component from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag in the root layout
- This follows the Next.js 13+ App Router pattern as documented in the official Vercel quickstart guide

#### `package.json`
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` as a dependency (version ^2.0.0)

#### `package-lock.json`
- Updated with the new dependency and its transitive dependencies

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I implemented the framework-specific instructions for Next.js 13.5+:

1. Imported the `SpeedInsights` component from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
2. Placed the component at the end of the body tag in the root layout file
3. This ensures Speed Insights will track Web Vitals across all pages in the application

## Verification Steps Completed

✅ **Build Verification**: Successfully ran `npm run build` - compilation completed without errors
✅ **Linting**: Ran `npm run lint` - no new errors introduced (only pre-existing warnings)
✅ **Dependencies**: Updated package-lock.json to ensure consistent dependency resolution

## Next Steps

To enable Speed Insights on Vercel:
1. Deploy this change to Vercel
2. Navigate to your project dashboard on Vercel
3. Go to the Speed Insights section
4. Click "Enable" to start collecting metrics
5. After deployment, the Speed Insights script will automatically be injected and begin tracking Web Vitals

## Technical Notes

- The `@vercel/speed-insights/next` package provides optimized integration with Next.js App Router
- The component is lightweight and only loads when deployed on Vercel
- No additional configuration is required beyond adding the component
- The integration automatically tracks Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID/INP, CLS)
